  "name": "TeamRetro: Email a weekly AI standup report to stakeholders",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 650,
        "content": "## TeamRetro: Email a weekly AI standup report to stakeholders\n\nFor product owners and managers who want the week's standups in one read. Every TeamRetro standup is stored in an n8n Data Table as it closes. Each Friday, OpenAI turns the week into a report on progress, blockers that lingered and risks for next week, and Gmail sends it, one email per team.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. **Daily:** the TeamRetro Trigger fires on **Standup Completed**. A delivery TeamRetro retries is skipped, so nothing happens twice. The day's updates become one plain-text row in the `standup_days` Data Table.\n2. **Fridays at 4 PM:** the schedule loads the `days` days before today from the table and groups them by team.\n3. OpenAI writes the report from only what the team said.\n4. The report is converted to HTML and emailed to `recipients`.\n5. Rows older than four weeks are pruned so the table stays small.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [ ] Create a Data Table named `standup_days` with columns: date, team, standup, transcript (strings), day, people (numbers)\n- [ ] Copy the Production URL from \"When Standup Closes\" into TeamRetro under Settings \u2192 Integrations \u2192 Webhooks, tick **Standup Completed**, and paste the signing secret back into the trigger\n- [ ] Set `recipients` in \"Report Settings\", and add OpenAI and Gmail credentials\n\nBoth flows have pinned samples. Running the pinned sample a second time stops at \"Skip Repeat Deliveries\": that is the duplicate guard. Standup text is sent to OpenAI, so check that suits your team.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the schedule's day and time, or `days` for a fortnightly report."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        364,
        124
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1176,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## 1. Store each closed standup\n\nFires when a standup closes and keeps the day as one Data Table row. Retries, and a second run of the pinned sample, stop at the duplicate check."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        364,
        644
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 956,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## 2. Load the week\n\nEvery Friday the `days` days before today come out of the Data Table and are grouped into one week per team."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1364,
        644
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1056,
        "height": 564,
        "content": "## 3. Write, send and tidy up\n\nOpenAI writes the report, Gmail sends it, and rows older than four weeks are pruned once per run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000010",
      "name": "When Standup Closes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-teamretro.teamRetroTrigger",
      "position": [
        460,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "events": [
          "standup.completed"
        ],
        "signingSecret": ""
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000009",
      "name": "Skip Repeat Deliveries",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.removeDuplicates",
      "position": [
        680,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "operation": "removeItemsSeenInPreviousExecutions",
        "dedupeValue": "={{ $json.deliveryId }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000012",
      "name": "Anyone Posted?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        900,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c12",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ ($json.data.standup.updates ?? []).length }}",
              "rightValue": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000013",
      "name": "Prepare the Day",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1120,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const standup = $('When Standup Closes').first().json.data.standup;\nconst lines = [];\nfor (const { participant, topics } of standup.updates) {\n  for (const { topic, updates } of topics) {\n    for (const update of updates) {\n      const carried = update.carriedForwardCount ? ` (carried over ${update.carriedForwardCount}x)` : '';\n      lines.push(`${participant.name || 'Anonymous'} [${topic.title}]: ${update.text}${carried}`);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// Exactly the Data Table's columns: the insert maps every field by name.\n// `day` (20260929) is what the weekly flow filters on; a number compares the same in every timezone.\nreturn [{ json: {\n  date: standup.date,\n  day: Number(standup.date.replace(/-/g, '')),\n  team: standup.team.name,\n  standup: standup.title || 'Standup',\n  people: standup.updates.length,\n  transcript: lines.join('\\n'),\n} }];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000014",
      "name": "Store the Day",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        1340,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {},
          "schema": [],
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "matchingColumns": [],
          "attemptToConvertTypes": false,
          "convertFieldsToString": false
        },
        "options": {},
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "standup_days"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000020",
      "name": "Every Friday at 4 PM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        460,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                5
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 16
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000021",
      "name": "Report Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        680,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "set-recipients",
              "name": "recipients",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "user@example.com, user@example.com"
            },
            {
              "id": "set-days",
              "name": "days",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000022",
      "name": "Load the Week",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        900,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "day",
              "keyValue": "={{ Number($now.minus({ days: $json.days }).toFormat('yyyyLLdd')) }}",
              "condition": "gte"
            },
            {
              "keyName": "day",
              "keyValue": "={{ Number($now.toFormat('yyyyLLdd')) }}",
              "condition": "lt"
            }
          ]
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "operation": "get",
        "returnAll": true,
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "standup_days"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000023",
      "name": "Group by Team",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1120,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const byTeam = {};\nfor (const { json: day } of $input.all()) (byTeam[day.team] ??= []).push(day);\n\nreturn Object.entries(byTeam).map(([team, days]) => {\n  days.sort((a, b) => a.day - b.day);\n  return { json: {\n    team,\n    days: days.length,\n    from: days[0].date,\n    to: days[days.length - 1].date,\n    week: days.map((d) => `### ${d.date}: ${d.standup}, ${d.people} posted\\n${d.transcript}`).join('\\n\\n'),\n  } };\n});"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000024",
      "name": "Write the Weekly Report",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1460,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Team: {{ $json.team }}. {{ $json.days }} standups from {{ $json.from }} to {{ $json.to }}.\n\n{{ $json.week }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "type": "SystemMessagePromptTemplate",
              "message": "You write a weekly standup report for stakeholders who did not attend. Reply in Markdown with exactly three sections: '## Progress' (what moved forward, at most 5 bullets), '## Blockers that lingered' (each blocker with who raised it and how many days it appeared; 'None.' if there were none) and '## Risks for next week' (at most 3 bullets, or 'None spotted.'). Use only what the standups say: never invent work, dates, owners or causes. Keep it under 250 words."
            }
          ]
        },
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.5
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000025",
      "name": "OpenAI GPT-5 Mini",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "position": [
        1460,
        1040
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000026",
      "name": "Format as HTML",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.markdown",
      "position": [
        1780,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "markdownToHtml",
        "options": {},
        "markdown": "={{ $json.text }}",
        "destinationKey": "html"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000027",
      "name": "Email Stakeholders",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "position": [
        2000,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Report Settings').first().json.recipients }}",
        "message": "={{ $json.html }}",
        "options": {
          "appendAttribution": false
        },
        "subject": "=Weekly standup report: {{ $('Group by Team').item.json.team }}, {{ $('Group by Team').item.json.from }} to {{ $('Group by Team').item.json.to }}",
        "emailType": "html"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1700-0000-0000-0000-000000000028",
      "name": "Prune Old Days",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        2220,
        820
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "day",
              "keyValue": "={{ Number($now.minus({ weeks: 4 }).toFormat('yyyyLLdd')) }}",
              "condition": "lt"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "deleteRows",
        "dataTableId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "standup_days"
        }
      },
      "executeOnce": true,
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
